# TWCA SSL Certification Authority — the intermediate www.tpex.org.tw omits.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   Some nodes behind the TPEx load balancer send only the leaf certificate in
#   the TLS handshake.  The leaf is issued by this intermediate, so OpenSSL
#   cannot build a path to any trust anchor and the handshake fails with
#   "unable to get local issuer certificate".  Python's requests does not
#   follow the leaf's AIA extension to fetch the missing link, so the only
#   options are to supply it ourselves or to stop verifying.  We supply it.
#
# WHY THIS IS NOT A TRUST DOWNGRADE
#   This certificate is itself issued by TWCA CYBER Root CA, which is already
#   in certifi's root store.  Anything it can vouch for was therefore already
#   trusted by our existing bundle — whenever a TPEx node bothers to send the
#   intermediate, verification succeeds with no help from us.  All this file
#   does is let OpenSSL *build* a path it would otherwise be unable to
#   complete.  The trust anchor is unchanged, and verification stays fully on.
#   Measured, not assumed: loading this file WITHOUT certifi's roots still
#   fails the handshake ("unable to get issuer certificate"), because OpenSSL
#   does not set X509_V_FLAG_PARTIAL_CHAIN and so still requires a self-signed
#   root at the top of the chain.  The anchor remains TWCA CYBER Root CA.
#
# PROVENANCE
#   Source      http://sslserver.twca.com.tw/cacert/Cyber_SSL_2023.crt
#               (the CA Issuers URI in the www.tpex.org.tw leaf's AIA extension)
#   Obtained    2026-09-14, DER, converted to PEM, no other modification.
#   Corroborated on the same day by a TLS handshake against a www.tpex.org.tw
#   node that *did* send a complete chain: the intermediate it served is
#   byte-identical to this file (same SHA-256).  Two independent paths, so the
#   plain-HTTP fetch above did not have to be trusted on its own.
#   Verified    signature of the www.tpex.org.tw leaf checks against this key;
#               this certificate's own signature checks against the certifi
#               copy of TWCA CYBER Root CA (SHA-256
#               3f63bb2814be174ec8b6439cf08d6d56f0b7c405883a5648a334424d6b3ec558).
#
# IDENTITY — asserted by tests/test_tls_chain.py, so replacing this file is a
# reviewable change and not something the network can do to us.
#   Subject     C=TW, O=TAIWAN-CA, OU=SSL Sub-CA, CN=TWCA SSL Certification Authority
#   Issuer      C=TW, O=TAIWAN-CA, OU=Root CA,    CN=TWCA CYBER Root CA
#   Serial      400134b04f0000000000000003e324ac
#   Validity    2023-02-23 07:22:24 UTC .. 2033-02-23 15:59:59 UTC
#   SHA-256(DER) 01af2324d098098f5e0cdf6faabada430b21cce777f47eacb26248b2fda3e531
#
# To replace it: fetch the new intermediate named by the current leaf's AIA,
# check its signature against a root already in certifi, drop it in here, and
# update the fingerprint in radar/tls.py.  Do not let anything do that at
# runtime.
